--- IR --->
# scoped to main, because the stdlib's own clamp bodies call minnum/maxnum further down and would
# otherwise satisfy checks meant for the calls written in this program
CHECK: define i32 @main(

# the same source spelling reaching two different intrinsics is the whole point of declaring each
# function at both precisions
CHECK: call double @llvm.sqrt.f64(double
CHECK: call float @llvm.sqrt.f32(float

# a one-overload-type, two-argument intrinsic, and the regression guard for this whole change: the
# overload-type vector used to be the *argument* list, so pow mangled as `llvm.pow.f64.f64` - a name
# LLVM never defined - and every intrinsic with more than one argument was undeclarable
#
# each check runs up to the `(` on purpose. `llvm.pow.f64` is a prefix of `llvm.pow.f64.f64`, so a
# check that stopped at the type would match the broken mangling too and assert nothing
CHECK: call double @llvm.pow.f64(double
CHECK: call double @llvm.copysign.f64(double

# three arguments, still one overload type
CHECK: call double @llvm.fma.f64(double

# and for integers it is signedness, not width, that picks the intrinsic
CHECK: call i32 @llvm.smin.i32(i32
CHECK: call i32 @llvm.umax.i32(i32
